 BSE|
 BSE| We can restrict the exciton descriptors to a specific direction,
 BSE| e.g. the x-components are:
 BSE|
 BSE|         d_eh^x   = | <x_h - x_e>_exc |
 BSE|
 BSE|         σ_e^x    = sqrt( <x_e^2>_exc - <x_e>_exc^2 )
 BSE|
 BSE|         σ_h^x    = sqrt( <x_h^2>_exc - <x_h>_exc^2 )
 BSE|
 BSE|         COV_eh^{μμ'} = <r^μ_e r^μ'_h>_exc - <r^μ_e>_exc <r^μ'_h>_exc
 BSE|
 BSE|         d_exc^x  = sqrt( | < |x_h - x_e|^2 >_exc )
 BSE|                  = sqrt( (d_eh^x)^2 + (σ_e^x)^2
 BSE|                          + (σ_h^x)^2 - 2 * (COV_eh^{xx}) )
 BSE|
 BSE| Subsequently, the cross-correlation matrix R_eh^{μμ'} is printed
 BSE|
 BSE|         R_eh^{μμ'} = COV_eh^{μμ'}/(σ^μ_e σ^μ_h) 
 BSE|
 BSE| Ref.: Eqs. (33)-(36)
 BSE| Phys. Rev. B 113, 205152 (2026); https://doi.org/10.1103/38k2-d55h
